  "plain": "The researcher Dean Radin, it is said, worked inside Stargate, a programme started by the CIA to test remote viewing, the claimed ability to see distant places with the mind, while having to speak badly of remote viewing in public. A guest named Maaneli Derakhshani passes this on, relaying that Radin \"was part of the project Stargate,\" and mentions Joe Rogan and the physicist Hal Puthoff along the way. If true, it would mean the public doubt was partly a cover for work the government took seriously."
